WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.100
Speaker 1: Well, we woke up to some delightful
news this morning.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.100
Lying.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:10.190
Disgraced Republican Congressman George Santos,
also known to many as George Anthony Devil

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.190
there.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.190
Santos.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.799
George Devil, older Anthony Devil, Older,
Anthony Santos and all.

00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:17.390
I think that covers most of the permutations.

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:22.910
He has been arrested and is in federal custody
as we speak, charged with 13 different criminal

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:23.910
counts.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.570
Isn't this fantastic news?

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:30.429
And we'll talk about the Trump $5 million
verdict in a moment.

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:33.290
What will happen to George Santos now that
he has been arrested?

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:37.160
Maybe this will get him out of Congress, which
would be delightful.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:42.130
CNN reports George Santos in federal custody
as feds.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.950
Feds unseal a 13 count indictment.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:45.950
We have a mug shot.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:47.180
It's an incredible thing.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:51.280
The Justice Department Wednesday unsealed
federal charges against Congressman George

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.770
Santos and the New York Republican is in custody.

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:55.810
Is in custody.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:01:01.559
Santos, whose astonishing pattern of lies
and fabrications stunned even hardened politicos,

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:06.880
has been charged on a 13 count indictment,
including seven counts of wire fraud, three

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:12.310
counts of money laundering, one count of theft
of public funds, and two counts of making

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:16.610
material materially false statements to the
House of Representatives.

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.720
This is just a delight.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.840
He was taken into custody in Melville on Long
Island, where the FBI is housed.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.140
From there, he was taken to a courthouse in
central Islip.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.860
He's expected to appear later today in federal
court.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.290
May already happen by the time you listen
to today's show or watch.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:38.570
The congressman's attorney declined to comment
to CNN spokespeople for the Brooklyn U.S.

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:39.720
Attorney's office.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.560
Justice Department and FBI also declined to
comment.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.650
One of my favorite things is that he seemed
not to even like know what was going on when

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:47.670
it was first mentioned to him.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.140
He's like, this is news to me.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:53.219
Santos was en route back to New York Tuesday
night, skipping house votes for the evening,

00:01:53.219 --> 00:01:54.360
according to a source.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:59.640
A spokeswoman for Santos, Naza Wilmer, wouldn't
respond to questions shouted from reporters

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.890
yesterday, abruptly departed the congressman's
office with a backpack.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:07.789
Prior to her departure from the office, CNN
witnessed three staffers abruptly depart with

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:08.810
their bags.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.140
They wouldn't talk.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.140
Can you imagine?

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:14.610
You're working for like the biggest liar in
Congress and now he's arrested.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.611
It's just a delight.

00:02:16.611 --> 00:02:20.230
House Speaker Kevin McCarthy said he's going
to look at the charges before determining

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:22.660
whether Santos should be removed from Congress.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:26.760
Quote, I'll look at the charges, he said to
CNN.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:30.560
Santos was spotted in the Capitol earlier
yesterday on his way in and out of McCarthy's

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:31.560
office.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.660
The speaker said he didn't know why Santos
was even there and that the congressman had

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.590
not told him personally about the charges.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:42.880
As you know, during his brief time in office,
Santos was accused of breaking campaign finance

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.140
laws violating violating federal conflict
of interest laws, stealing cash meant for

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:52.569
an Iraq war veterans dying, dog masterminding
a credit card fraud scheme, and lying about

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:54.840
where he went to school and where he worked.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:59.670
And I would add to that lying about his athletic
achievements and lying about so many different

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:00.750
things.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.709
This is this is really great.

00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:09.549
And it's not great as some on the right will
say, because I just want my political enemies

00:03:09.549 --> 00:03:16.159
to have weaponized justice proceedings against
them when there is no evidence they've done

00:03:16.159 --> 00:03:17.159
anything wrong.

00:03:17.159 --> 00:03:19.120
It's actually quite the opposite.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:26.269
There is so much material about the wrongdoing
of Jorge Santos, including all sorts of different

00:03:26.269 --> 00:03:27.450
criminality.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.540
What's good is that he's being held accountable.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:37.159
He's not being excused from wrongdoing because
he is one of 435 members of Congress, members

00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:38.330
of the House of Representatives.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:42.700
Better said one of 535 members of both houses
of Congress.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.700
That's good.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.709
When people are held accountable, that's a
good thing.

00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:48.319
The Associated Press reporting about this
as well.

00:03:48.319 --> 00:03:52.799
There's one particular moment that I love
that this is so good.

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:54.829
Reached on Tuesday, Santos said.

00:03:54.829 --> 00:03:56.020
This is news to me.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:00.720
The AP called him to say, Hey, what do you
think about all the charges in your forthcoming

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:01.720
arrest?

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:02.720
He was like news to me.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.690
I don't know anything about it, he said in
a brief phone interview.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:07.079
You're the first to call me about it.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:09.810
That is just just absolutely the best.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:12.709
So we're going to follow this very closely.

00:04:12.709 --> 00:04:14.640
There are two stories here.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:20.350
There is the story of the charges and the
wrongdoing itself on the one hand.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:24.639
And then there is the story of what do Republicans
do?

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:29.340
Many Republicans have wanted this guy out
for a while, but it wasn't really clear they

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:31.110
had the whole party behind them.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:33.610
And so they kind of said, listen, we have
a process.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:38.880
I don't know if we really have the votes or
whatever, and they kind of shut up about it.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.669
And it to a degree, it went away.

00:04:41.669 --> 00:04:45.940
You then had other Republicans who very much
want to get this guy out.

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:49.890
It wasn't clear they had a path to do it before
these charges.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.310
Maybe now they do.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:56.169
It's important to remember charges are merely
allegations.

00:04:56.169 --> 00:05:00.080
In the United States, you're innocent until
proven guilty in a court of.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:01.080
Law.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:06.360
However, there are many jobs where if you
are charged with certain crimes, you are at

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.100
minimum suspended from your job.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:13.720
And then if you are in the future acquitted,
then there are different processes.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:18.360
Again, it's different depending on the military
would be one thing.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:23.060
Financial services companies have other policies,
so on and so forth.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:29.560
There is latitude from employers of different
kinds as to how charges are handled, given

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:32.630
that charges themselves are not actually guilty
verdicts.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:35.729
And that's the system we have, and that's
a good thing.

00:05:35.729 --> 00:05:37.320
What do Republicans do now?

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.320
I don't know.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:39.650
But we'll be watching it.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:06:57.360
And delightful news to wake up to.

